        "# 06 · Architecture benchmark (lecturer track, performance only)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Question.** Is the Transformer earning its place? GRU-D, an LSTM and a minimal RWKV are trained under the same protocol and compared with the models of Phase 2: our softmax Transformer (`softmax_s42`), the KA-Transformer (`ka_s42`) and LightGBM (`gbdt_iculos`).\n",
        "\n",
        "**This notebook makes no interpretability claim** and none of its models enters notebooks 03–05. It is one of the optional performance analyses of the pre-registration (section 12): FIT and VAL only, no reserved fold.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Protocol (identical to 01 / 02).** Frozen subject split; FIT-only preprocessing; each stay's most recent 168 h (`runs.predict_store`); same labels and horizons (t+1, t+3, t+6); focal loss; warmup + cosine schedule; early stopping (patience 8, at most 24 epochs); checkpoint soup. Every baseline is given what the Transformer is given: forward-filled values, the observed mask, the time since the last measurement, the static variables and the ICU hour.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Tuning, stated plainly.** Each baseline gets the same grid of three learning rates, tried at the primary seed and chosen on VAL; every other setting is the Transformer's, and model sizes are fixed in `sepsis_core/baselines.py`. **Our Transformer had 30 Optuna trials on the same VAL fold** (v3), the baselines have 3. Any tuning advantage is therefore the Transformer's, and a baseline that matches it does so with one tenth of the search.\n",
        "\n",
        "Seeds: 3 per baseline (42, 1042, 2042). The VAL score of the chosen learning rate at seed 42 is a maximum over three runs and is slightly optimistic; the other two seeds are not. Aggregates only."
      ]
    },
